            "body": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Our founder, Mr Yik, grew up in his father’s shoe factory in Singapore, learning the trade at the workbench in the 1970s. Fresh out of national service, he took over the reins from his father at 20. To further his skills, he took on an apprenticeship in shoemaking, learning the science and art behind what makes a shoe comfortable. More than forty years later, he’s still obsessed with every detail, from the last to the materials and the fit. To him, comfort can’t be standardised. No two feet are alike, so no single size can fit everyone.</p><p>Soon after taking over, he moved production overseas to stay competitive on price. But he refused to give up making shoes in-house. Keeping design and production under our own control meant we could still answer for the quality and workmanship of every pair. It also let us design our own lasts for Asian feet, especially catered for Singapore market, in extreme, half and wide sizes.</p><p>In 1989, we started making uniform shoes for the organisations behind Singapore’s frontline: nurses, cabin crew and bus captains, people who are on their feet for an entire shift. These clients taught us what a long day demands of a shoe. It has to look smart with a uniform, grip on wet floors, and stay supportive and comfortable from the first hour to the last. Our dedication to quality and comfort earned us many long-standing customers, including major healthcare, transport and aviation organisations across Singapore.</p><p>The business grew with its clients. From a husband-and-wife operation, it expanded to a team of ten and set up its own delivery fleet to reach customers across the island. Today, we supply more than 80 corporate clients across healthcare, aviation, transport and F&amp;B, handling specialised sizing, customisation and bulk orders from start to finish. More than a million pairs have now been made and fitted.</p><p>Now in our third generation, we have opened our doors to everyone. At our first flagship store in City Square Mall, anyone can walk in, have both feet measured for length and width, and try the same shoes Singapore’s frontline teams wear every day. Our shoes now come in more designs, colours and styles to suit every occasion, with the same comfort built in.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "paragraph",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "enable_mobile_size": false,
                "mobile_font_size": "1rem",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
